{:edb/db-before-t 1546 :edb/db-after-t 1547 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534859 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:18:04.593Z" 13194139534859 true] [17592186083153 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315513 13194139534859 true] [17592186087780 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315530 13194139534859 true] [17592186100789 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315516 13194139534859 true] [17592186100792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315537 13194139534859 true] [17592186100830 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315506 13194139534859 true] [17592186110512 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315544 13194139534859 true] [17592186115302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315523 13194139534859 true] [17592186152105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315551 13194139534859 true] [17592186315506 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315507 13194139534859 true] [17592186315506 1089 "q-123699" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315506 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534859 true] [17592186315506 1100 "What is the limit of the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}-1?$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315506 1113 #uuid "ca8b6c60-d3e5-5453-9458-79ebc1aabeff" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315506 1145 "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nWe calculate the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}-1)=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}=-1+0=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sequence converges and its limit is $-1.$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315508 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315509 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315510 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315511 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315512 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1041 "selection" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315511 13194139534859 true] [17592186315507 1110 #uuid "1d105b68-3533-5781-a926-8c0c96e958b8" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315508 1034 "The sequence diverges." 13194139534859 true] [17592186315508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315508 1111 #uuid "4a1a568c-100d-58a8-bb67-2b2c61335cce" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315509 1034 "1" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315509 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315509 1111 #uuid "42ce795e-5972-57c4-80df-b3fe60008618" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315510 1034 "0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315510 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315510 1111 #uuid "a08d14bb-d059-5cc7-a1a8-375af38c60fc" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315511 1034 "-1" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315511 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315511 1111 #uuid "2d35eb1c-6228-5be6-b4c0-10dd5f8f764b" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315512 1034 "-2" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315512 1111 #uuid "37df9160-b0e2-5797-be5a-3015107a11ad" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315513 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315514 13194139534859 true] [17592186315513 1089 "q-282168" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315513 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534859 true] [17592186315513 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $f(y)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $5.$ Find $f(y).$\n\n$f(y)=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315513 1113 #uuid "69bfecff-a4c9-53af-810f-8c9439557c4f" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315513 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) & =(5)(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i})) & =5({y}^{2}-(2+3\\text{i})y-(2-3\\text{i})y+(2+3\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-(2+3\\text{i}+2-3\\text{i})y+({2}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2})) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-4y+(4+9)) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-4y+13) \\\\  & =5{y}^{2}-20y+65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(y)=5{y}^{2}-20y+65.$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315514 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315515 13194139534859 true] [17592186315514 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534859 true] [17592186315514 1041 "field-1" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315514 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315515 13194139534859 true] [17592186315514 1110 #uuid "e259043b-f98d-5de3-90d0-7adcd5da5b12" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315515 1034 "5y^2-20y+65" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315515 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315515 1111 #uuid "2e1393ae-93cc-522f-a225-ff5eba1e79fc" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315517 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315519 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315521 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1089 "q-337668" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1100 "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1113 #uuid "edafa2b5-0c55-598b-8ba1-9ebc55335790" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315516 1145 "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315518 13194139534859 true] [17592186315517 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534859 true] [17592186315517 1041 "field-1" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315517 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315518 13194139534859 true] [17592186315517 1110 #uuid "a06c6805-870e-56ee-8e96-88e115ada4c7" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315518 1034 "4\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315518 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315518 1111 #uuid "e0f21b7e-5339-5b54-a9b8-41f04585b70e" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315520 13194139534859 true] [17592186315519 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534859 true] [17592186315519 1041 "field-2" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315519 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315520 13194139534859 true] [17592186315519 1110 #uuid "b060abd8-45d0-5064-ad6b-483e0db53ed5" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315520 1034 "-1" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315520 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315520 1111 #uuid "0ce9bff4-1e58-5e5c-bfea-c5f84eea1f93" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315522 13194139534859 true] [17592186315521 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534859 true] [17592186315521 1041 "field-3" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315521 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315522 13194139534859 true] [17592186315521 1110 #uuid "c6c8a442-9c73-567d-8c41-f7880e3cb806" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315522 1034 "0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315522 1111 #uuid "0cd20774-9c5e-5470-9b57-386b0b0f1768" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315523 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315524 13194139534859 true] [17592186315523 1089 "q-47675" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315523 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534859 true] [17592186315523 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/assets/dd8697532367aa85a521d4af3af6f9184e89964f2619ee4dc4ffe84d21877f31.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315523 1113 #uuid "3b0f90fb-bc0c-512a-b9f1-eee634aeb642" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315523 1145 "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-4$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a corner, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=4$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-4$, $x=0$, and $x=4.$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315525 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315526 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315527 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315528 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315529 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1041 "selection" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315525 13194139534859 true] [17592186315524 1110 #uuid "db81b04a-cbc0-5292-aa6c-ee07d857b021" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315525 1034 "$x=-4$, $x=0$ and $x=4$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315525 1111 #uuid "ab9d9885-11f8-59ce-94f6-1de0f9b8a353" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315526 1034 "$x=0$ only" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315526 1111 #uuid "b6947e43-d9f4-5b79-bc3a-e1dbb825a3e8" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315527 1034 "$x=-4$ only" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315527 1111 #uuid "60e76c3e-b2e2-5a30-bd0c-5d935a82dc0e" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315528 1034 "$x=4$ only" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315528 1111 #uuid "3000dd67-6539-5c32-adce-41e65bb77280" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315529 1034 "$x=-4$ and $x=4$ only" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315529 1111 #uuid "87f95ba7-3a8e-54d7-9060-880ec7bc0934" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315531 13194139534859 true] [17592186315530 1089 "q-69563" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534859 true] [17592186315530 1100 "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1?$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315530 1113 #uuid "8ca29321-6dcb-5eb2-8ac4-99202a87781f" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315530 1145 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315532 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315533 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315534 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315535 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315536 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1041 "selection" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315535 13194139534859 true] [17592186315531 1110 #uuid "951051d0-8b82-59b1-84f1-e677f7e96b3f" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315532 1034 "$7\\sqrt{2}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315532 1111 #uuid "dac783cd-66d9-5e60-b99c-f692fb526bb9" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315533 1034 "$7$ and $2$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315533 1111 #uuid "c5461de7-327c-52e0-b5c8-b080f14e4a23" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315534 1034 "$7$ and $4$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315534 1111 #uuid "7d48c214-18a0-5b8b-8c83-f780b7a346bb" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315535 1034 "$14$ and $4$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315535 1111 #uuid "f9541b9f-c045-5de1-afc5-5387cd71f7a0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315536 1034 "$14\\sqrt{2}$ and $4\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534859 true] [17592186315536 1111 #uuid "4482e558-90fa-53b9-806a-8c75bac14a8a" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315537 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315538 13194139534859 true] [17592186315537 1089 "q-69940" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315537 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534859 true] [17592186315537 1100 "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315537 1113 #uuid "0c794907-2a8c-5720-b1b4-1f1e6bf16096" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315537 1145 "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 2-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-2+2 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315539 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315540 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315541 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315542 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315543 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1041 "selection" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315543 13194139534859 true] [17592186315538 1110 #uuid "58b7b164-c435-5e81-af37-0d79f3949c95" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315539 1034 "3" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315539 1111 #uuid "d01bb27d-91a7-5098-8f57-aa35b86d86d0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315540 1034 "8" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315540 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315540 1111 #uuid "af31d06a-cf3e-5b53-9d24-db0347176fe6" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315541 1034 "2" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315541 1111 #uuid "c50fa07f-01f5-5330-a426-99614d47fbff" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315542 1034 "1" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315542 1111 #uuid "3bbeec9c-b1d3-59bd-9e76-516e2842f77e" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315543 1034 "0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315543 1111 #uuid "3939d455-97d5-5fa1-a197-91a515d3a1a6" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315544 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315545 13194139534859 true] [17592186315544 1089 "q-70781" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315544 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534859 true] [17592186315544 1100 "Which of the following values is in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315544 1113 #uuid "553a2492-7880-54fb-8193-a269d45e9e5d" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315544 1145 "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/assets/d7984b9098d02bfc2b1e9a422aef919533abce54fbb94117e709c7613b0870a3.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nTherefore, of the given values, only $y=1$ is in the range of the function." 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315546 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315547 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315548 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315549 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315550 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1041 "selection" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315549 13194139534859 true] [17592186315545 1110 #uuid "f96b5dc3-7d83-5a5a-94b8-fd23d06acd3d" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315546 1034 "-5" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315546 1111 #uuid "f685487a-e321-540c-ba7a-b0d6cea134fd" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315547 1034 "-2\\pi " 13194139534859 true] [17592186315547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315547 1111 #uuid "12c49739-05ab-5796-ad83-a8778a932547" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315548 1034 "\\pi " 13194139534859 true] [17592186315548 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315548 1111 #uuid "f9f1b7a0-0a0b-57e6-87e4-761b0ca30a9d" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315549 1034 "1" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315549 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315549 1111 #uuid "9032cce5-dc4d-55c6-aa9e-1e26837ea8c4" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315550 1034 "5" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315550 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315550 1111 #uuid "e71f59e8-da7d-549f-9db5-1934ad7bffd6" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315551 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315552 13194139534859 true] [17592186315551 1089 "q-77893" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315551 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534859 true] [17592186315551 1100 "Consider the line $2x-y-4=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315551 1113 #uuid "0966918f-fe74-55cf-9f19-d48b021374b5" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315551 1145 "First, notice that the line $2x-y-4=0$ passes through the points $R(0,-4)$ and $S(1,-2)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $R$ and $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${R}^{′}(8,-12)$ and ${S}^{′}(3,-6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${R}^{′}$ and ${S}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-12) & =\\frac{-6-(-12)}{3-8}(x-8) \\\\ y+12 & =-\\frac{6}{5}(x-8) \\\\ 5y+60 & =-6x+48 \\\\ 6x+5y+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315553 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315554 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315555 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315556 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315557 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1041 "selection" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315555 13194139534859 true] [17592186315552 1110 #uuid "cd18d463-d93f-53ae-bdbb-266d99b693e8" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315553 1034 "6x-5y+12=0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315553 1111 #uuid "44dd6e4f-cda6-58d7-b4d1-716ddcc3df47" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315554 1034 "5x-6y+12=0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315554 1111 #uuid "e8c36d31-3476-5948-a639-8c4dc49d7acc" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315555 1034 "6x+5y+12=0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315555 1111 #uuid "2cb4685a-afbb-50e0-afe6-4b2938a0001c" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315556 1034 "5x-6y-2=0" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534859 true] [17592186315556 1111 #uuid "0ee27f95-0c44-5083-bd9e-857f75a2af62" 13194139534859 true] [17592186315557 1034 "5x+6y-12=0" 13194139534859 tru